    "https://wku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205297": {
      "title": "Manager, Budget- ARCH Institute",
      "description": "Western Kentucky University\nJob Posting: Manager, Budget- ARCH Institute Western Kentucky University \n\tJob Posting: Manager, Budget- ARCH Institute Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Manager, Budget- ARCH Institute Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Dean CHHS Locations: Bowling Green, KY Posted: Sep 29, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 994700 Position ID: 205297 Share About Western Kentucky University: Western Kentucky University (WKU) is a student-centered, applied-research institution committed to providing its students with a transformative academic and social experience and to elevating its surrounding communities. Founded in 1906, WKU is the third largest public four-year institution in the Commonwealth of Kentucky with approximately 16,293 students and nearly 2,612 faculty and staff employees. Western Kentucky University is committed to empowering its campus community. At the heart of our mission, we seek to provide holistic education and employment experiences that prepare students, faculty, and staff to become effective scholars, contributors, and leaders in our ever-evolving communities. Located 65 miles north of Nashville, TN, and just over 100 miles south of Louisville, KY, WKU's main campus is in Bowling Green, KY - a city with approximately 70,000 residents. Our population is ethnically diverse, with more than 85 languages spoken in and around Bowling Green, and people from 35 nationalities call our community home. Western Kentucky University seeks to attract talented faculty and staff who are inspired individually to contribute to WKU's strategic plans and ongoing success. We offer comprehensive wellness and health benefits to employees and their families, including domestic partners and other qualified dependents and take pride in providing a workplace culture that supports balancing the responsibilities of work and family life. Paid-time off for holidays, vacation and sick leave, and a tuition discount program for employees and dependents are also provided. Learn more about WKU and Bowling Green at wku.edu/about . Job Description: The CAYA Advancing Research and Community Health (ARCH) Institute in Western Kentucky University's College of Health and Human Services is seeking applications for a Manager, Budget- ARCH Institute. The Budget Manager will support the fiscal and administrative operations of the applied research centers and labs housed within the Community Health Sciences Complex. The position will work closely with center directors, principal investigators, faculty, staff, and university administrative offices to support the effective management of operating funds, grants, contracts, purchasing, personnel transactions, and other financial activities. The Budget Manager must be able to establish priorities, manage multiple responsibilities, and work independently to meet deadlines. A qualified candidate will be organized, detail-oriented, and capable of working effectively in a busy, collaborative environment. The Budget Manager must handle financial and administrative information with discretion while demonstrating accuracy, integrity, accountability, and professionalism. The successful candidate should possess strong analytical, decision-making, and problem-solving skills, along with proficiency in Microsoft Office applications-particularly Microsoft Excel and excellent written and verbal communication skills. The Budget Manager will report to the Director of the ARCH Institute. This is a revenue dependent position. Continuation is dependent upon funding/need. The Budget Manager will provide expert guidance to ARCH Institute leadership on budget planning, financial operations, and the fiscal management of grants and contracts. They will exercise independent judgment to analyze complex financial matters, recommend solutions, and advise on decisions that have a significant impact on the Institute's operations and sustainability. While not exhaustive, the following duties are expected for this position. Responsibilities may be modified based on the operational needs of the CAYA ARCH Institute, its affiliated centers and labs, and the College of Health and Human Services. Financial Administration Monitor and reconcile operating, grant, and contract fund accounts. Review financial transactions for accuracy and completeness. Process journal entries and support the management of center and sponsored-project budgets. Track expenditures against approved budgets and facilitate budget-reallocation requests. Prepare financial reports for principal investigators, center directors, and Institute leadership to support planning and informed decision-making. Assist with the development of annual operating budgets and financial projections. Grant and Contract Support Monitor sponsored-project budgets, expenditures, and overall spending activity. Review grant and contract expenditures for allocability, allowability, and alignment with approved budgets and applicable requirements. Track financial and programmatic reporting deadlines and work with principal investigators and center and lab leadership to support timely submissions. Maintain complete and accurate documentation for sponsored-project transactions and related financial activities. Assist center directors and principal investigators with contract budget review and coordinate with the Office of Sponsored Programs and other university offices as needed. Accounts Payable and Procurement Facilitate purchase requisitions, payment requests, and other accounts-payable processes. Process and reconcile procurement-card transactions through J.P. Morgan PaymentNet. Facilitate the purchase of equipment, supplies, and services needed for research, service, and administrative activities. Track encumbrances, outstanding commitments, and pending transactions. Payroll and Personnel Transactions Assist with the preparation and processing of employee personnel action forms. Process labor redistributions and other payroll-related adjustments as needed. Assist with the preparation and submission of Form 16 documentation. Facilitate faculty fellow assignments, including contract preparation and distribution, as needed. Assist with Interview Exchange requisitions and administrative components of the hiring process. Compliance and Contract Support Assist with monitoring financial and administrative compliance requirements associated with grants and contracts. Review and maintain supporting documentation to promote compliance with university policies, sponsor requirements, and applicable regulations. Identify potential financial or administrative concerns and work with Institute leadership and appropriate university offices to support timely resolution. Administrative Coordination Serve as a fiscal liaison among the ARCH Institute, affiliated research centers and labs, and university administrative offices. Facilitate financial documents, required approvals, and administrative processes involving faculty, staff, and central university offices. Assist with university travel processes, including travel authorizations, arrangements, and reimbursement vouchers, as needed. Maintain organized and accessible financial and administrative records for the Institute and its affiliated centers and labs. Perform other related duties in support of the ARCH Institute's fiscal and administrative operations. Requirements: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. Experience with financial administration, budgeting, accounting, grants management, or a closely related area. Demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, particularly Microsoft Excel. Strong organizational, analytical, communication, and problem-solving skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities, maintain accurate records, meet deadlines, and work collaboratively with individuals across multiple administrative and academic units. Additional Information: Salary Range:  $55,308 - $57,000 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Application Instructions: The following items must be submitted through this electronic talent management system: Cover Letter Resume Unofficial Transcripts You will receive email confirmation that your submission has been received. The candidate review process will generally begin as materials are received. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Western Kentucky University 1906 College Heights Blvd. Bowling Green, KY 42101"
