    "https://wku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204885": {
      "title": "Analyst, Prospect Strategy",
      "description": "Western Kentucky University\nJob Posting: Analyst, Prospect Strategy Western Kentucky University \n\tJob Posting: Analyst, Prospect Strategy Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Analyst, Prospect Strategy Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Advancement Services Locations: Bowling Green, KY Posted: Sep 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 995327 Position ID: 204885 Share About Western Kentucky University: Western Kentucky University (WKU) is a student-centered, applied-research institution committed to providing its students with a transformative academic and social experience and to elevating its surrounding communities. Founded in 1906, WKU is the third largest public four-year institution in the Commonwealth of Kentucky with approximately 16,293 students and nearly 2,612 faculty and staff employees. Western Kentucky University is committed to empowering its campus community. At the heart of our mission, we seek to provide holistic education and employment experiences that prepare students, faculty, and staff to become effective scholars, contributors, and leaders in our ever-evolving communities. Located 65 miles north of Nashville, TN, and just over 100 miles south of Louisville, KY, WKU's main campus is in Bowling Green, KY - a city with approximately 70,000 residents. Our population is ethnically diverse, with more than 85 languages spoken in and around Bowling Green, and people from 35 nationalities call our community home. Western Kentucky University seeks to attract talented faculty and staff who are inspired individually to contribute to WKU's strategic plans and ongoing success. We offer comprehensive wellness and health benefits to employees and their families, including domestic partners and other qualified dependents and take pride in providing a workplace culture that supports balancing the responsibilities of work and family life. Paid-time off for holidays, vacation and sick leave, and a tuition discount program for employees and dependents are also provided. Learn more about WKU and Bowling Green at wku.edu/about . Job Description: Position Summary The Division of Philanthropy & Alumni Engagement (PAE) seeks to foster lifelong relationships with WKU constituents through activities designed to honor the WKU spirit, engage all members of the WKU family in the life of the University, and secure private support to advance WKU's mission. The Division's core values drive our success through: Positivity, Accountability, and Excellence. The Prospect Strategy Analyst reports to the Executive Director of Strategic Operations & Appeals and works with the Prospect Strategy Assistant Director to manage donor prospecting and research activities at Western Kentucky University. This position supports the prospect management and research needs of approximately 7 full-time fundraising professionals as well as research needs of campus partners. Responsibilities include the identification, research, and analysis of alumni, parents, and friends in support of fundraising efforts at WKU. This position utilizes a variety of sources and research tools to update prospect records and provide recommendations of philanthropic prospects, and assists by providing information needed to make data-informed strategic decisions. Essential Job Functions: The following duties are customary for this position, but are not to be construed as all-inclusive. Duties may be added, deleted and assigned based on management discretion and institutional needs. Prospect Research Work with leadership and fundraisers to define needs, share results, and enhance the value and effective use of research in identifying, qualifying, cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding donors. Conduct detailed research as requested by major gifts and principal gifts team members. Execute prospect identification activities for new prospects utilizing external information and prospect research tools and databases. Produce prospect and donor profiles and event bios when needed to support cultivation and solicitation activities. Integrate newly identified prospects into the allocated prospect discovery pool for qualification and assignment. Manage research queue and assign out requests to other team members as needed. Recommends prospect research tools and technologies to Executive Director for budget inclusion. Track research productivity with database metrics and project management tools. Conduct research using public, proprietary, purchased or leased databases, newspapers, published materials, and other resources to identify potential donors and funding sources. Utilize prospecting tools such as data screening and modeling to provide analyses of targeted groups and overall prospect pool. Prospect Management Provide support to the Assistant Director of Prospect Strategy with portfolios as needed, including portfolio audits and the assignment review process. Utilize data to make meaningful and strategic recommendations for prospecting of portfolios. Participate in portfolio management and business planning meetings. Support Prospect Strategy and Data Analyst to manage prospect records in database system and performs regular audits of prospect data. Contribute to the planning and implementation of comprehensive, proactive prospect identification and management of potential prospects. Conduct verification on wealth screening files and make portfolio assignment recommendations. Foster collaboration and partnerships Assist others on the team and/or across the Division on special projects to support the Division needs as necessary. Build partnerships across campus to drive PAE initiatives. Support best practices Collaborate with team members and recommend improvements. Research best practices; evaluating and learning new tools to support philanthropic and alumni engagement needs. Contribute outside-the-box ideas in conjunction with research and best practices to position the Division to be leaders in the industry. Creates job-specific SOPs (standard operating procedures) to document process to create consistency and continuity as needed. Knowledge and Skills Considered Essential for Success: Must be a self-starter, organized and able to work in a team environment. Ability to establish priorities and work independently. Research skills necessary to locate and validate information from multiple sources including websites, social media, and commercial research databases. Advanced problem-solving and critical-thinking skills. Ability to manage to completion large, long-term or fast-moving projects. Strong attention to detail and accuracy with data entry and project tracking. Strong grammar and writing skills. Superior and effective interpersonal, written, and verbal communication and presentation skills. Computer literacy and proficiency, including Microsoft Office Suite with high proficiency in Excel and aptitude for learning new software packages. Knowledge of commercial research databases such as Lexis Nexis. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage large volumes of data in an accurate and meaningful way. Experience with data analysis and reporting. Ability to use discretion in working with sensitive, confidential materials and data. Requirements: Bachelor's degree Additional Information: Salary Range:  $39,100 - $45,000 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact the Office of Institutional Equity at 270-745-5121 for assistance. To report concerns related to WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy, No. 0.2040 and/or WKU's Sex and Gender-Based Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Policy, No. 0.2070, please complete the Discrimination, Harassment, and Retaliation Reporting Form . Additional information regarding Title IX, including contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and reporting options,  is available on WKU's Title IX website . Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: https://www.wku.edu/academics/ For information related to job postings, application status, or the hiring process, please email employment@wku.edu . Application Instructions: The following items must be submitted through this electronic talent management system: Cover Letter Resume You will receive email confirmation that your submission has been received. The candidate review process will generally begin as materials are received. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Western Kentucky University 1906 College Heights Blvd. Bowling Green, KY 42101"
    },
    "https://wku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204673": {
      "title": "Specialist, Museum Development",
      "description": "Western Kentucky University\nJob Posting: Specialist, Museum Development Western Kentucky University \n\tJob Posting: Specialist, Museum Development Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Specialist, Museum Development Category: Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Kentucky Museum Locations: Bowling Green, KY Posted: Sep 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 995372 Position ID: 204673 Share About Western Kentucky University: About the Kentucky Museum The Kentucky Museum opened in 1939 as a place for \"Kentuckians to know Kentucky.\" Today, the Kentucky Museum continues this charge while increasing interdisciplinary knowledge of, appreciation, and respect for a collection representative of Southcentral Kentucky. As a teaching museum part of Western Kentucky University, we conduct research and preserve and interpret artifacts in a variety of fields, with special emphasis on fine, decorative, and folk arts; clothing and textiles; toys; political memorabilia; and other culturally significant items from our community. About Western Kentucky University Western Kentucky University (WKU) is a student-centered, applied-research institution committed to providing its students with a transformative academic and social experience and to elevating its surrounding communities. Founded in 1906, WKU is the third largest public four-year institution in the Commonwealth of Kentucky with approximately 16,293 students and nearly 2,612 faculty and staff employees. Western Kentucky University is committed to empowering its campus community. At the heart of our mission, we seek to provide holistic education and employment experiences that prepare students, faculty, and staff to become effective scholars, contributors, and leaders in our ever-evolving communities. Located 65 miles north of Nashville, TN, and just over 100 miles south of Louisville, KY, WKU's main campus is in Bowling Green, KY - a city with approximately 70,000 residents. Our population is ethnically diverse, with more than 85 languages spoken in and around Bowling Green, and people from 35 nationalities call our community home. Western Kentucky University seeks to attract talented faculty and staff who are inspired individually to contribute to WKU's strategic plans and ongoing success. We offer comprehensive wellness and health benefits to employees and their families, including domestic partners and other qualified dependents and take pride in providing a workplace culture that supports balancing the responsibilities of work and family life. Paid-time off for holidays, vacation and sick leave, and a tuition discount program for employees and dependents are also provided. Learn more about WKU and Bowling Green at wku.edu/about . Job Description: Position Summary The Museum Development Specialist advances the Kentucky Museum's fundraising, grant development, external relations and communications, and exhibitions planning and execution activities. The position researches and develops funding opportunities, writes grant proposals, cultivates relationships with funders and community partners, supports the museum's membership and development initiatives, and guides exhibitions through the planning and creation process. Exhibition work will include helping museum staff identify guest curators, manage project schedules and budgets, facilitate communication between internal staff and external partners, and support the successful development and implementation of exhibitions. Primary/Key Responsibilities Development, Grant Writing, and Funding (50%) Work with Museum Director, museum staff, and WKU Philanthropy to identify funding priorities and translate museum exhibitions, programs, education initiatives, collections, research, and other activities into persuasive funding proposals. Research, identify, and pursue grant and fundraising opportunities from foundations, government agencies, corporations, individuals, or other potential fundraising sources. Work with museum director and WKU Philanthropy staff to identify funding opportunities. Stay up to date on emerging trends in funding opportunities related to museums, higher education, arts, humanities, and cultural organizations. Write compelling grant proposals, letters of inquiry, project narratives, budgets, supporting documents, and other funding materials. Manage grant submission calendars, deadlines, reporting requirements, renewals, and other deliverables. This includes ensuring principal investigators complete any needed reports and documentation. Exhibition Project Management (30%) Responsible for managing the development of exhibitions by leading the exhibitions committee, identifying guest curators (often WKU faculty) and other external collaborators, and managing timelines. Assist museum staff in identifying and evaluating potential guest curators whose expertise aligns with proposed exhibition themes and museum priorities. Serve as exhibits and special projects manager, coordinating project schedules, meetings, contracts, deliverables, budgets, and communications in collaboration with museum staff. Coordinate purchasing supplies required for exhibition creation. Ensure guest curators and external collaborators know the museum's processes and policies. Facilitate communication between guest curators, external collaborators, and museum staff. Document exhibitions committee meetings, project decisions, assignments, and deadlines, ensuring all team members are kept up-to-date throughout the project. Assist with writing, editing, designing, and coordinating exhibition labels, interpretive panels, educational materials, exhibition descriptions, website copy, press materials, and other audience-focused content. Provide editorial and project-management support for exhibition content and team while recognizing that primary curatorial responsibility may rest with the assigned curator or guest curator. Communications and Membership (20%) Develop the museum's regular external communications, including press releases, member communications, and social media content that informs public audiences about the museum's exhibitions, programs, activities, and institutional priorities. Collaborate with the Museum Director to cultivate and steward membership through our existing membership program. Manage museum's Adopt-an-Artifact campaign to continue raising funds for collections care Other Responsibilities Participate in museum staff meetings, planning activities, and institutional initiatives. Share duties related to departmental purchasing, including acquiring quotes and working with agents in the WKU Purchasing Department. Along with museum staff, work occasional evening and weekend museum events outside regular work hours. This is not a remote or hybrid job. Work will be physically conducted at WKU's main campus. Occasional independent travel required to meet with donors and/or external collaborators and make public presentations. Other duties as assigned. Requirements: Bachelor's degree in nonprofit management, communication, humanities, social studies, museum studies or related field. Minimum three years professional, post-undergraduate, experience in grant writing, non-profit development, and/or fundraising. Demonstrated experience securing funding from foundations, corporations, government agencies, individuals, or other funders. Demonstrated experience writing successful grant proposals, funding requests, and writing for a public audiences. Experience developing project budgets, schedules, and funding plans. Must possess a valid driver's license. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of museum exhibition development standards and procedures. Strong project management and organizational abilities, including the ability to manage multiple deadlines and follow budgets and priorities involving multiple team members. Excellent writing and editing skills with strong attention to detail. Ability to collaborate with museum staff and external partners, including providing and accepting constructive feedback. Must be able to lift 50 lbs. Additional Information: Salary Range: $47,000 -$50,000 Kentucky state law requires all public institutions of postsecondary education to conduct pre-employment criminal background checks to determine suitability for employment. Western Kentucky University (WKU) is committed to a policy and practice of providing equal employment and educational opportunities to all individuals. In accordance with Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Revised 1992, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, no form of discrimination or harassment will be tolerated at WKU on the basis of race, color, ethnicity, national origin, creed, religion, political belief, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, marital status, age, uniformed services, veteran status, genetic information, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, or physical or mental disability in admission to career and technical education programs and/or activities, or employment practices. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, should notify the office of Institutional Equity. To request an accommodation, report a complaint, or ask questions regarding WKU's Discrimination and Harassment Policy (#0.2040), please contact Ms. Ena Demir, Executive Director/Title IX Coordinator via email at ena.demir@wku.edu or by phone at (270) 745-6867. Ms. Demir is also responsible for coordinating the University's response to complaints related to sex and gender harassment. Additional information regarding Title IX is accessible via WKU's https://www.wku.edu/titleix/ website. Information concerning educational programs offered by WKU are provided at: http://www.wku.edu/atwku/academics.php For information related to job postings, please email employment@wku.edu . Application Instructions: The following items must be submitted through this electronic talent management system: Cover Letter Resume You will receive email confirmation that your submission has been received. The candidate review process will generally begin as materials are received. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Western Kentucky University 1906 College Heights Blvd. Bowling Green, KY 42101"
    }
  },
